-- title:
--   Transport of the Drinfeld form under a semilinear endomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $W$ a commutative integral domain and $t \in W$ non-zero. Let $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units, and suppose $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1)$ lies in $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Write $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(t)\,v - f\,u)$, and let $\theta : S \to S$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $\sigma : W \to W$ be a ring homomorphism with $\sigma(w) - w \in (t)$ for every $w \in W$, let $w_1 \in W$ satisfy $\sigma(t) = t\,w_1$, and assume $\theta$ acts on the image of each constant $C(w)$ by $C(\sigma(w))$. Let $M \in M_2(W)$ be such that, for each $j$, the difference of $\theta$ applied to the image of $X_j$ and the image of $\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by the images of $X_0$ and $X_1$. Then, in $(W/(t))[X_0,X_1]$, the residue of $w_1$ times $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ equals the result of substituting $X_j \mapsto \sum_i \overline{M_{ij}}\,X_i$ into $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$.
--
--   This is the leading-form transport identity for a Drinfeld chart ring in the Katz–Mazur local model $t\,v = f\,u$: modulo $t$, the linear part of a $\sigma$-semilinear endomorphism multiplies the Drinfeld (Dickson) form by the residue of $\sigma(t)/t$. It is used in the computation of the action of inertia on the Drinfeld charts of integral models of full-level modular curves, in the two lemmas identifying that action, up to the relevant normalisation, with a unipotent diagonal element.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_smul_drinfeldForm_eq_aeval_linearPart_of_ringHom_semilinear.lean

